% ⚑ AND THE TIER WENT BACK TO sandbox, WHICH IS THE POINT OF Ζ·wheel·backend.  This was briefly
% `toolchain` because the builder shelled out to `uv`, a host binary no sandbox stages — the
% honest tier for a check that genuinely needs the host.  Declaring the PEP 517 backend removed
% that need: the builder now imports setuptools from a pinned, hashed pip dependency Bazel
% stages, so the wheel builds IN the sandbox with no exemption.  Measured, and it is the tier
% that makes the check meaningful — a wheel built against the live tree proves nothing about a
% wheel built from declared inputs, which is exactly the false green this arc found (the library
% was in the artifact only because `uv` ran unsandboxed).
@misc{bnd-wheel,
  section  = {engine},
